1
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:20,520
They say there are no secrets in this world.

2
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:24,880
Is it true that the people in Creative are having an affair?

3
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:26,880
Keep your voice down.

4
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:30,480
Walls have ears.

5
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:34,200
Someone’s chat screenshots just got leaked yesterday.

6
00:00:34,520 --> 00:00:37,240
Come on! You can hide nothing here.

7
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:40,240
You can, if you’re good enough.

8
00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:44,960
Do you think Dan can close the deal this time?

9
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:47,800
I feel bad for him.

10
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:50,920
With a budget this big, the pressure must be insane.

11
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:54,880
But as a top-selling AE,

12
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:56,840
I think he’ll pull it off.

13
00:00:57,480 --> 00:00:59,560
That’s true.

14
00:00:59,560 --> 00:01:01,240
Not even two years here,

15
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:02,680
and he’s a top performer every month.

16
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:03,360
Right.

17
00:01:04,959 --> 00:01:06,760
But my secret…

18
00:01:07,320 --> 00:01:09,640
-doesn’t even need to be dug up.
-Let’s gossip after some snacks.

19
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:11,320
It just spills out on its own

20
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:16,039
like a nosebleed

21
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:20,760
that strikes whenever I’m under pressure.

22
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:24,160
And it always happens on important days.

23
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:26,320
But whatever.

24
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:28,800
I can handle it.

25
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:31,240
Just wipe it away quickly,

26
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:33,039
and no one will ever know.

27
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:36,280
Congratulations to our scholarship student,

28
00:01:36,280 --> 00:01:38,840
Mr. Danusorn Promsri.

29
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:51,360
I kept my secret hidden…

30
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:53,560
to make my life look as perfect as possible.

31
00:01:56,479 --> 00:01:57,560
Stand a little closer.

32
00:01:57,560 --> 00:02:00,160
I graduated with first-class honors

33
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:02,200
from a top university.

34
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:04,080
Many juniors looked up to me.

35
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:05,240
Thank you.

36
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:07,000
P’Dan!

37
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:09,639
Wow, is this for me?

38
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:12,320
-Isn’t it cute?
-It’s so cute and huge.

39
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:14,760
-Thank you.
-Let’s take a picture.

40
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:20,160
P’Dan.

41
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:22,600
Could you give us a CEO pose?

42
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:23,960
Act cool.

43
00:02:24,079 --> 00:02:24,760
Sure.

44
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:34,160
What kind of CEO can’t afford a cup of coffee?

45
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:38,880
How about this pose? It’s cuter.

46
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:40,480
It really is cute.

47
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:42,079
Three, two, one!

48
00:02:42,079 --> 00:02:46,760
P’Dan, P’Dan, P’Dan!

49
00:02:58,440 --> 00:03:00,640
Why should we hire you?

50
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:02,160
Honestly,

51
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:04,040
I’d love to say…

52
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:05,720
because I’m amazing.

53
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:09,240
But I don’t want to get kicked out just yet, so I’ll say…

54
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:11,480
If someone gives me an opportunity,

55
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:13,480
I’ll make it so worthwhile

56
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:15,400
that they’ll never regret it.

57
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:24,320
Congratulations!

58
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:29,840
Congrats!

59
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:30,920
Thank you.

60
00:03:31,160 --> 00:03:32,360
Great job.

61
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:33,800
You deserve it.

62
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:35,000
Thank you, everyone,

63
00:03:35,680 --> 00:03:36,760
for coming to surprise me.

64
00:03:41,920 --> 00:03:43,000
These days,

65
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:45,760
whenever people look at me, this is all they see.

66
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:50,400
The perfect image I created.

67
00:04:19,519 --> 00:04:21,519
Nong Dan!

68
00:04:21,519 --> 00:04:22,280
Oh!

69
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:23,720
Your shirt…

70
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:30,680
It’s gorgeous.

71
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:33,760
Don’t tell me it’s from the new collection.

72
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:36,320
Yes.

73
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:37,840
It’s the latest collection.

74
00:04:38,120 --> 00:04:39,040
Oh gosh!

75
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:40,520
It’s fabulous.

76
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:43,120
I’ll see you later then.

77
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:43,880
Sure.

78
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:47,200
How is everyone doing?

79
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:54,800
Hello.

80
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:56,880
I’m Dan, Danusorn Promsri,

81
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:58,840
the Account Executive for this project.

82
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:00,960
So, let’s get started.

83
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:04,600
The concept for this project is ‘Driving Beyond Luxury’.

84
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:07,720
We want to make driving more than just luxury.

85
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:09,760
We’re keeping the luxury aspect,

86
00:05:09,760 --> 00:05:11,960
but we’ll push more driving experience.

87
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:14,240
Our target group is the new generation.

88
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:17,560
This gen values the driving experience,

89
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:18,560
so it should be fun,

90
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:19,800
safe,

91
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:21,600
and reliable.

92
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:22,600
Thank you.

93
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:35,440
You did it!

94
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:36,040
Yeah.

95
00:05:36,280 --> 00:05:37,840
Did you see their faces?

96
00:05:38,280 --> 00:05:40,520
No wonder you’re our company’s no.1 AE.

97
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:42,840
You’re amazing.

98
00:05:42,840 --> 00:05:43,280
Right.

99
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:44,560
What should we eat today?

100
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:45,880
Teach me how.

101
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:47,720
You’re already doing well.

102
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:52,880
And the Top Salesperson of the Month Award

103
00:05:52,880 --> 00:05:54,320
goes to…

104
00:05:59,520 --> 00:06:01,400
Mr. Dan!

105
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:05,000
Thank you.

106
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,320
Great job.

107
00:06:06,720 --> 00:06:07,520
Thank you.

108
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:27,680
Guys,

109
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:29,120
I’m heading home now.

110
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:30,680
Bye bye.

111
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:31,440
See you.

112
00:06:31,440 --> 00:06:32,159
Bye bye.

113
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:37,400
Six o’clock sharp.

114
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:40,480
Bag on point.

115
00:06:41,320 --> 00:06:42,600
Outfit on point.

116
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:44,960
Leave on time.

117
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:48,360
My work life was almost perfect,

118
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:49,280
if it weren’t for…

119
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:52,040
my new teammate.

120
00:06:52,520 --> 00:06:53,320
He’s great at his job,

121
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:56,120
but even better at running his mouth.

122
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:57,159
That's Saint.

123
00:08:00,440 --> 00:08:02,000
Use this one.

124
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,280
His new song is out!

125
00:08:03,280 --> 00:08:04,400
Is it good?

126
00:08:06,720 --> 00:08:08,720
Have you heard his new song yet?

127
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:09,440
Who?

128
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:11,240
Oh.

129
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:12,240
Everyone,

130
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:16,440
we have a new member joining us.

131
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:18,040
This is Saint,

132
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:19,160
our new AE.

133
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,600
Let's clap.

134
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:24,160
A new guy?

135
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:26,000
He’s so cute and puppy-like.

136
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:26,720
I know right.

137
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,760
It’s not every day

138
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:30,840
we get a handsome guy joining our team.

139
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:32,080
I’m loving this.

140
00:08:32,760 --> 00:08:33,480
Hello.

141
00:08:33,679 --> 00:08:34,799
I’m Saint.

142
00:08:35,360 --> 00:08:36,600
I'll be in your care.

143
00:08:38,360 --> 00:08:39,640
Welcome!

144
00:08:41,720 --> 00:08:43,520
That desk is yours.

145
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:44,240
Yes.

146
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:47,200
You’re sitting across from our top-selling AE.

147
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:49,920
Make sure you learn from that talented senior.

148
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:51,360
Thank you.

149
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:52,160
Good luck.

150
00:08:54,520 --> 00:08:55,400
Wow.

151
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:58,040
He’s even more handsome up close.

152
00:08:58,920 --> 00:09:00,440
Yeah, he’s gorgeous.

153
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:02,840
I’m folding.

154
00:09:03,560 --> 00:09:04,760
Enough. Stop staring.

155
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:05,960
Dan.

156
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:08,960
I’m leaving him in your hands.

157
00:09:09,280 --> 00:09:12,040
Saint is probably a year younger than you.

158
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:14,360
Take good care of him.

159
00:09:14,360 --> 00:09:16,400
and teach him the job.

160
00:09:17,400 --> 00:09:18,000
Understood.

161
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:20,920
Hello.

162
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:23,400
Hello.

163
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:09,440
Thank you.

164
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:27,080
Thank you.

165
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:28,520
Dan.

166
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:30,560
It’s “P’Dan”!

167
00:10:32,160 --> 00:10:32,720
Yeah.

168
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:33,520
P’…?

169
00:10:34,240 --> 00:10:34,960
Dan.

170
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:54,520
Nong Saint.

171
00:10:55,200 --> 00:10:57,160
Please call me…

172
00:10:57,520 --> 00:10:58,760
P’Dan.

173
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:02,840
Does this office have a SOTUS system?

174
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:06,160
Should I report this to HR?

175
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:07,080
Don’t be ridiculous.

176
00:11:07,280 --> 00:11:09,680
This is about treating each other with respect.

177
00:11:10,160 --> 00:11:11,200
Then,

178
00:11:12,080 --> 00:11:13,200
P’Dan,

179
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:16,280
when were you born?

180
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:18,920
April 30, 1999.

181
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:22,280
I was born on November 13, 1999.

182
00:11:25,400 --> 00:11:27,360
So you’re…

183
00:11:29,280 --> 00:11:30,800
not even a year older than me.

184
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:32,160
Right?

185
00:11:33,480 --> 00:11:34,840
I graduated before you,

186
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:36,520
so I’m your senior.

187
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:41,040
But technically, you’re just…

188
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:42,920
my mentor.

189
00:11:46,280 --> 00:11:47,680
Then could my mentor teach me…

190
00:11:48,560 --> 00:11:51,440
how to be the top-selling AE every month?

191
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:53,720
And I mean…

192
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:55,400
some pretty close guidance.

193
00:11:57,520 --> 00:11:59,080
The first thing I’m going to teach you

194
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:02,120
is how to show your coworkers some respect.

195
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:05,600
You little pup.

196
00:12:50,720 --> 00:12:51,840
I’m freezing.

197
00:14:11,680 --> 00:14:12,400
See?

198
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:15,280
That was the beginning of the bad blood

199
00:14:15,280 --> 00:14:16,520
between me and Saint.

200
00:14:17,040 --> 00:14:18,600
That email address is wrong.

201
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:20,600
Then check this one for me.

202
00:14:22,840 --> 00:14:23,480
Saint.

203
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:24,640
Take this.

204
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:28,600
Yes.

205
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:34,800
Saint.

206
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:35,480
Here.

207
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:37,200
Saint.

208
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:38,000
Saint.

209
00:14:38,320 --> 00:14:38,840
Saint.

210
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:39,520
Saint.

211
00:14:42,520 --> 00:14:44,600
Hurry up. We need to submit this.

212
00:14:45,280 --> 00:14:45,960
Dan.

213
00:14:45,960 --> 00:14:46,520
Yes?

214
00:14:46,520 --> 00:14:47,960
Could you sign this for me?

215
00:14:48,200 --> 00:14:49,400
-Okay.
-Thank you.

216
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:54,160
Take this one too.

217
00:15:01,800 --> 00:15:02,720
Dan.

218
00:15:02,920 --> 00:15:06,480
The client wants five more slides.

219
00:15:06,480 --> 00:15:08,040
-I’ve forwarded you the email.
-Okay.

220
00:15:08,040 --> 00:15:08,880
Thanks a lot.

221
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:13,200
Saint.

222
00:15:13,840 --> 00:15:15,640
I’ve forwarded the task to you.

223
00:15:15,920 --> 00:15:16,640
Please take a look.

224
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:22,720
Nong Dan.

225
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:23,200
Yes?

226
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:25,520
Can you help me pick an intern?

227
00:15:25,520 --> 00:15:26,960
What do you think?

228
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:28,760
This one looks sophisticated.

229
00:15:28,920 --> 00:15:30,520
This one looks capable.

230
00:15:30,520 --> 00:15:32,720
And this one is as pretty as I am.

231
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:36,160
-I think…
-Which one should we pick?

232
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:40,400
I think Saint should choose.

233
00:15:40,800 --> 00:15:41,760
Let him do it.

234
00:15:41,760 --> 00:15:42,760
You want Nong Saint to choose?

235
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:44,280
Okay.

236
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:46,400
Nong Saint, come take a look.

237
00:15:46,600 --> 00:15:49,280
Which intern should we pick?

238
00:15:49,520 --> 00:15:50,600
You want me to choose?

239
00:15:50,880 --> 00:15:51,640
Of course.

240
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:52,960
How about this?

241
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:54,920
I’ll count down from five…

242
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:55,720
Four.

243
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:56,720
Three.

244
00:15:56,800 --> 00:15:57,400
Two.

245
00:15:58,440 --> 00:15:59,200
Just kidding.

246
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:01,400
Take your time.

247
00:16:01,400 --> 00:16:02,200
I’ll be back.

248
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:12,160
I can’t stand Dan!

249
00:16:36,400 --> 00:16:37,200
You know that…

250
00:16:39,520 --> 00:16:42,800
you can’t take confidential documents home, right?

251
00:16:46,720 --> 00:16:48,160
What makes you think I don’t know?

252
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:49,920
That’s good, then.

253
00:16:50,520 --> 00:16:52,200
I’m just making sure it doesn’t leak.

254
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:57,480
I’m professional enough.

255
00:16:57,800 --> 00:16:59,840
I don’t need a probationary newbie lecturing me.

256
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:02,520
As for these documents,

257
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:04,599
I’m taking them to Accounting.

258
00:17:05,040 --> 00:17:05,680
Got it?

259
00:17:08,599 --> 00:17:09,440
Bye bye.

260
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:18,160
You’ve complained about Saint for three months.

261
00:17:18,440 --> 00:17:19,280
Aren’t you tired of it?

262
00:17:19,839 --> 00:17:21,440
That puppy is so annoying.

263
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:23,400
He messes with the AC

264
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:25,400
and keeps getting on my nerves in meetings.

265
00:17:26,319 --> 00:17:26,920
Hey.

266
00:17:28,560 --> 00:17:30,680
He’s got you worked up, huh?

267
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:31,440
What?

268
00:17:31,680 --> 00:17:32,800
Do you have a crush on Saint?

269
00:17:32,880 --> 00:17:33,920
Do you?

270
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:34,840
Are you crazy?

271
00:17:35,080 --> 00:17:36,200
Hey.

272
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:39,160
I’m sure you’ve got a thing for that puppy.

273
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:39,720
What?

274
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:41,280
Nonsense.

275
00:17:41,440 --> 00:17:42,920
Look at you, all shy.

276
00:17:42,920 --> 00:17:44,240
I’m not. Just eat.

277
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:46,080
Why do you hate him so much?

278
00:17:46,840 --> 00:17:47,720
I mean...

279
00:17:48,360 --> 00:17:49,440
Saint is handsome.

280
00:17:49,920 --> 00:17:50,800
His eyes smile.

281
00:17:51,120 --> 00:17:53,920
And he’s cute when his ears turn red.

282
00:17:53,920 --> 00:17:55,040
What’s cute about that?

283
00:17:55,280 --> 00:17:57,200
And when he secretly adjusts the AC,

284
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:59,080
I’ve seen him sneaking glances at you.

285
00:17:59,240 --> 00:18:01,880
He’s just afraid I’ll nag him.

286
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:04,160
He knows I’m always cold,

287
00:18:04,160 --> 00:18:05,360
yet he keeps turning it down.

288
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:06,840
So annoying.

289
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:08,560
You’re acting weird.

290
00:18:09,280 --> 00:18:10,360
Don’t tell me…

291
00:18:11,680 --> 00:18:13,080
He wants some encouragement.

292
00:18:14,680 --> 00:18:17,920
SaintDan! SaintDan! SaintDan!

293
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:18,920
Stop!

294
00:18:19,160 --> 00:18:20,080
That’s enough.

295
00:18:20,920 --> 00:18:21,840
There’s nothing going on.

296
00:18:22,040 --> 00:18:22,840
Eat your food.

297
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:24,320
Keep your voice down.

298
00:18:24,320 --> 00:18:26,120
SaintDan.

299
00:18:26,320 --> 00:18:28,600
So... Dan is really the opposite of you.

300
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:31,280
The office atmosphere is pretty fun.

301
00:18:31,800 --> 00:18:34,080
Even though I’m a newbie, I never feel lonely

302
00:18:34,320 --> 00:18:37,840
because everyone’s always inviting me to do things.

303
00:18:39,280 --> 00:18:42,120
For example, Mew is a great coworker.

304
00:18:42,120 --> 00:18:43,640
She’s always cheering me on.

305
00:18:44,320 --> 00:18:47,160
Oui gives me the latest gossip every lunch break.

306
00:18:47,520 --> 00:18:49,440
Mostly about other people’s business,

307
00:18:49,760 --> 00:18:51,520
with only a little work talk.

308
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:54,360
And I also play MOBA games with New.

309
00:18:55,280 --> 00:18:56,560
I don't want to work with Dan again!

310
00:18:57,200 --> 00:18:57,840
Saint.

311
00:18:58,560 --> 00:19:00,040
Come to my office for a moment.

312
00:19:07,160 --> 00:19:09,680
I’ve reviewed your performance over the past three months.

313
00:19:10,160 --> 00:19:13,080
You’ve improved much faster than expected.

314
00:19:13,640 --> 00:19:15,840
I’ll confirm you’ve passed probation

315
00:19:15,840 --> 00:19:17,360
at the end of the month,

316
00:19:17,360 --> 00:19:19,960
and take the team out this Friday to celebrate.

317
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:22,280
Thank you, P’Ta.

318
00:19:23,680 --> 00:19:24,880
So, how’s everything?

319
00:19:25,240 --> 00:19:27,880
Settled in with your teammates?

320
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:29,040
Anything you’d like to tell me?

321
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:32,200
Everything’s great.

322
00:19:32,520 --> 00:19:34,000
Your makeup looks lovely today.

323
00:19:34,680 --> 00:19:35,440
Gorgeous.

324
00:19:36,040 --> 00:19:37,240
Let’s take a photo for our stories.

325
00:19:37,240 --> 00:19:38,080
Sure.

326
00:19:38,800 --> 00:19:39,920
Hey, hey.

327
00:19:39,920 --> 00:19:41,320
Why are you two taking a photo alone?

328
00:19:41,560 --> 00:19:43,400
Everyone, come join us.

329
00:19:43,600 --> 00:19:45,600
I'm coming.

330
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:46,200
Saint.

331
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:47,920
Come take a photo with us.

332
00:19:47,920 --> 00:19:49,080
Ready?

333
00:19:49,080 --> 00:19:50,160
One second.

334
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:51,440
Ready.

335
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:52,840
Come on.

336
00:19:52,840 --> 00:19:54,320
Want to do a Gen Z pose?

337
00:19:54,320 --> 00:19:55,720
Gen Z? How?

338
00:19:55,720 --> 00:19:56,720
Teach us.

339
00:19:56,800 --> 00:19:57,800
Say Brazil.

340
00:19:57,800 --> 00:19:58,600
Brazil.

341
00:19:58,600 --> 00:19:59,800
One, two, three.

342
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:05,320
Saint.

343
00:20:08,960 --> 00:20:09,960
You got this.

344
00:20:15,920 --> 00:20:18,080
(Good luck, newbie.)

345
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:30,040
Saint, This way!

346
00:20:30,680 --> 00:20:31,680
That was close.

347
00:20:31,840 --> 00:20:33,040
Damn.

348
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:34,320
You keeps stealing my kills.

349
00:20:34,320 --> 00:20:37,520
My name speaks for itself.

350
00:20:37,520 --> 00:20:39,800
So, how are things with Dan?

351
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:43,120
You’re about the same age.

352
00:20:43,120 --> 00:20:44,680
You should be closer, right?

353
00:20:58,600 --> 00:20:59,440
Oh, Dan.

354
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:00,800
I was going to ask for your…

355
00:21:08,560 --> 00:21:09,720
Hey, that’s brilliant!

356
00:21:09,960 --> 00:21:11,120
I love it.

357
00:21:12,520 --> 00:21:13,520
I think it’s a great idea.

358
00:21:13,800 --> 00:21:14,680
It can’t go wrong.

359
00:21:15,160 --> 00:21:17,320
Everyone gets the wrong idea sometimes.

360
00:21:25,080 --> 00:21:25,840
Quite good.

361
00:21:27,120 --> 00:21:27,720
Wonderful.

362
00:21:30,680 --> 00:21:31,760
Oh, Dan.

363
00:21:31,760 --> 00:21:32,840
Perfect timing.

364
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:34,160
Have a seat.

365
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:37,080
I wanted to discuss something with you both.

366
00:21:46,840 --> 00:21:49,280
Our company just landed a major project

367
00:21:49,280 --> 00:21:51,240
worth tens of millions.

368
00:21:51,600 --> 00:21:53,440
The client wants our agency

369
00:21:53,440 --> 00:21:55,840
to handle the campaign directly.

370
00:21:57,120 --> 00:21:59,040
It’s a new mall

371
00:21:59,040 --> 00:22:01,720
under Siam Central Group.

372
00:22:02,360 --> 00:22:07,400
We need our strongest team on this.

373
00:22:08,200 --> 00:22:09,800
I need people I can trust,

374
00:22:15,880 --> 00:22:18,880
so I’ll let Dan and Saint handle the project.

375
00:22:19,440 --> 00:22:21,920
You two will work together.

376
00:22:21,920 --> 00:22:24,080
No exceptions.

377
00:22:28,920 --> 00:22:30,120
I understand, P’Ta,

378
00:22:30,800 --> 00:22:33,120
but I’m concerned about time management.

379
00:22:33,520 --> 00:22:35,160
With a project this big,

380
00:22:35,160 --> 00:22:36,680
the workload will be enormous.

381
00:22:36,800 --> 00:22:38,440
Without proper planning,

382
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:41,040
the team will burn out before we finish.

383
00:22:41,560 --> 00:22:43,760
I’m confident you two can handle it.

384
00:22:44,720 --> 00:22:48,320
Dan, you have proven yourself time and again.

385
00:22:48,560 --> 00:22:50,680
And Saint’s been improving remarkably fast.

386
00:22:50,680 --> 00:22:52,920
It’s a perfect pairing.

387
00:22:57,040 --> 00:22:59,320
If that’s what the company wants,

388
00:23:01,280 --> 00:23:02,200
I’ll do it.

389
00:23:03,160 --> 00:23:03,880
Good.

390
00:23:04,040 --> 00:23:05,960
This is an opportunity for the company

391
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:08,080
and for both of you.

392
00:23:08,760 --> 00:23:10,800
I want you to do it together.

393
00:23:14,280 --> 00:23:15,280
Of course, P’Ta.

394
00:23:16,480 --> 00:23:17,240
Excellent.

395
00:23:17,480 --> 00:23:20,000
Be ready for the kick-off meeting

396
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:22,880
tomorrow at nine.

397
00:23:22,880 --> 00:23:24,280
I’ll lay out the timeline for you.

398
00:23:26,240 --> 00:23:27,080
Got it.

399
00:23:46,040 --> 00:23:47,640
P’Ta wants me on a project with Dan.

400
00:23:48,120 --> 00:23:48,680
Huh?

401
00:23:48,680 --> 00:23:49,200
Hey!

402
00:24:02,520 --> 00:24:03,920
P’Ta wants me on a project with Saint.

403
00:24:06,160 --> 00:24:07,240
Sorry, sorry.

404
00:24:07,400 --> 00:24:08,200
I was too shocked.

405
00:24:09,040 --> 00:24:09,760
Seriously?

406
00:24:10,200 --> 00:24:11,840
You have to work with the newbie?

407
00:24:12,200 --> 00:24:13,160
Good luck.

408
00:24:13,160 --> 00:24:14,920
Prince Dan will surely give you a hard time.

409
00:24:17,240 --> 00:24:19,040
But you’re a top seller.

410
00:24:19,280 --> 00:24:20,680
This is a piece of cake, right?

411
00:24:21,440 --> 00:24:22,400
Of course.

412
00:24:22,800 --> 00:24:24,720
As long as he doesn’t run his mouth,

413
00:24:24,920 --> 00:24:26,200
we should be fine.

414
00:24:27,080 --> 00:24:29,200
But Saint seems nice.

415
00:24:29,440 --> 00:24:30,680
You really don’t like him?

416
00:24:30,960 --> 00:24:31,840
He's too cheeky.

417
00:24:32,200 --> 00:24:33,400
Bring it on.

418
00:24:33,400 --> 00:24:34,600
If he comes at me, I’ll hit back.

419
00:24:34,920 --> 00:24:36,560
Just keep your cool.

420
00:24:36,560 --> 00:24:38,520
Don’t fight before the project even starts.

421
00:24:39,240 --> 00:24:41,560
Defeating the top seller won’t be easy.

422
00:24:42,320 --> 00:24:43,920
The rule for being a top seller is simple.

423
00:24:44,200 --> 00:24:45,440
Close the deal.

424
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:47,080
Just you wait.

425
00:24:47,280 --> 00:24:49,720
I’m taking him down.

426
00:25:11,800 --> 00:25:12,720
Wait for me!

427
00:25:19,240 --> 00:25:20,200
Thanks.

428
00:25:22,080 --> 00:25:22,800
Dan.

429
00:25:22,960 --> 00:25:24,520
About yesterday’s presentation deck,

430
00:25:24,520 --> 00:25:25,520
-I think—
-Sorry.

431
00:25:26,560 --> 00:25:28,720
I don’t discuss work outside the office.

432
00:25:29,080 --> 00:25:30,280
It’s unprofessional.

433
00:25:43,720 --> 00:25:44,640
Hey, Saint.

434
00:25:47,600 --> 00:25:48,960
An Americano, as usual.

435
00:25:49,120 --> 00:25:50,800
I waited in line for half an hour .

436
00:25:50,800 --> 00:25:52,560
Take it, or I’ll be offended.

437
00:25:52,720 --> 00:25:53,560
Just take it.

438
00:25:53,560 --> 00:25:54,160
It’s hot.

439
00:25:54,200 --> 00:25:55,320
Let’s get back to work.

440
00:25:55,560 --> 00:25:56,680
Come on, let’s go.

441
00:26:00,120 --> 00:26:00,800
Thank you.

442
00:26:03,680 --> 00:26:05,000
That was amazing.

443
00:26:05,080 --> 00:26:06,040
Finally, it’s done.

444
00:26:07,280 --> 00:26:08,600
It went well.

445
00:26:08,920 --> 00:26:10,320
Thank you so much, Dan.

446
00:26:10,520 --> 00:26:11,320
My pleasure.

447
00:26:11,800 --> 00:26:12,480
Dan!

448
00:26:12,680 --> 00:26:14,040
Could you check this file for me?

449
00:26:14,040 --> 00:26:15,760
The client just replied.

450
00:26:15,760 --> 00:26:16,600
I need it ASAP.

451
00:26:16,600 --> 00:26:17,040
Sure.

452
00:26:17,040 --> 00:26:17,680
Okay.

453
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:22,080
You forwarded it to me, right?

454
00:26:22,080 --> 00:26:23,000
Yes.

455
00:26:23,080 --> 00:26:24,080
Okay.

456
00:26:24,080 --> 00:26:25,160
Let me check the file.

457
00:26:26,480 --> 00:26:27,440
Let’s see.

458
00:26:27,440 --> 00:26:28,960
What needs updating?

459
00:26:35,080 --> 00:26:35,880
All done.

460
00:26:36,560 --> 00:26:37,840
Thank you.

461
00:26:37,840 --> 00:26:38,560
No problem.

462
00:26:50,680 --> 00:26:51,680
Uh, Dan.

463
00:26:52,280 --> 00:26:53,160
Could you help me with—

464
00:26:53,200 --> 00:26:54,080
Sorry.

465
00:26:54,560 --> 00:26:56,280
I don’t work outside office hours.

466
00:27:09,800 --> 00:27:11,280
You spoiled rich kid.

467
00:27:25,120 --> 00:27:26,400
Oh, Mr. Dan!

468
00:27:27,560 --> 00:27:29,320
Hello.

469
00:27:29,320 --> 00:27:30,200
Where are you off to?

470
00:27:30,200 --> 00:27:31,040
I’m heading home.

471
00:27:31,400 --> 00:27:32,720
Drive safe.

472
00:27:32,720 --> 00:27:33,800
After you.

473
00:27:34,600 --> 00:27:37,280
I’d open the door, but I’m afraid of damaging your car.

474
00:27:37,920 --> 00:27:39,080
Here.

475
00:27:39,680 --> 00:27:40,320
Goodbye.

476
00:27:40,320 --> 00:27:41,560
Goodbye, sir.

477
00:27:43,040 --> 00:27:45,560
Security, at your service.

478
00:27:45,840 --> 00:27:47,440
What a spoiled rich kid.

479
00:27:47,560 --> 00:27:48,960
This way.

480
00:28:03,320 --> 00:28:04,080
Sir.

481
00:28:05,400 --> 00:28:06,920
Can I help you?

482
00:28:09,320 --> 00:28:12,320
Sneaking around like that.

483
00:28:12,920 --> 00:28:14,040
Are you a thief?

484
00:28:15,240 --> 00:28:17,120
What kind of thief?

485
00:28:17,560 --> 00:28:19,200
Do I look like one?

486
00:28:20,440 --> 00:28:21,600
Then move along.

487
00:28:32,680 --> 00:28:34,040
Think you’re so high?

488
00:28:37,120 --> 00:28:38,560
Think you’re so mighty?

489
00:28:42,200 --> 00:28:43,440
Think you’re so rich?

490
00:28:47,360 --> 00:28:48,800
Think you’re so cute?

491
00:28:55,080 --> 00:28:56,400
Why am I thinking about him?

492
00:28:57,000 --> 00:28:58,160
Stop. Stop right there.

493
00:28:58,800 --> 00:29:00,080
Stop thinking.

494
00:30:00,040 --> 00:30:01,720
I’ve transferred your allowance for this month.

495
00:30:02,960 --> 00:30:03,680
Is it enough?

496
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:05,200
I saw it.

497
00:30:05,440 --> 00:30:06,320
It’s enough.

498
00:30:06,800 --> 00:30:07,920
Anything else you want?

499
00:30:10,600 --> 00:30:12,920
No, nothing.

500
00:30:13,600 --> 00:30:15,560
Have the twins agreed to go to extra classes yet?

501
00:30:16,200 --> 00:30:18,400
They can be a little stubborn,

502
00:30:18,400 --> 00:30:19,800
but they agreed to go.

503
00:30:21,440 --> 00:30:22,840
If you need anything, just let me know.

504
00:30:23,320 --> 00:30:24,200
Okay.

505
00:30:49,840 --> 00:30:52,400
(I’ve booked a dinner reservation. Let’s meet up.)

506
00:31:33,080 --> 00:31:34,600
I have to say…

507
00:31:35,360 --> 00:31:37,240
you’ve done a very thorough job.

508
00:31:37,680 --> 00:31:38,920
The analysis is solid,

509
00:31:39,200 --> 00:31:40,080
and all the information is there.

510
00:31:42,120 --> 00:31:43,800
But the problem is...

511
00:31:43,800 --> 00:31:46,400
these reports are completely different.

512
00:31:47,440 --> 00:31:49,600
You’ve clearly worked separately.

513
00:31:50,320 --> 00:31:52,400
You haven’t talked at all, have you?

514
00:31:53,000 --> 00:31:54,440
I’ve tried talking to Dan,

515
00:31:56,320 --> 00:31:57,400
but I’m not sure

516
00:31:57,760 --> 00:31:59,160
if he wants to talk to me.

517
00:31:59,600 --> 00:32:01,840
I only discuss things that matter.

518
00:32:01,840 --> 00:32:03,760
If it’s just pointless chatter,

519
00:32:04,040 --> 00:32:04,840
I’m not interested.

520
00:32:06,920 --> 00:32:07,600
Hold on.

521
00:32:08,040 --> 00:32:10,920
This project is worth tens of millions.

522
00:32:10,920 --> 00:32:13,800
If you two keep this up, it’s doomed.

523
00:32:14,080 --> 00:32:15,920
I’ve passed probation.

524
00:32:15,920 --> 00:32:17,320
You must have seen

525
00:32:17,320 --> 00:32:20,480
how I always do my best in every task.

526
00:32:21,080 --> 00:32:22,040
But what can I do now?

527
00:32:23,880 --> 00:32:26,560
A certain someone won’t even talk to me.

528
00:32:27,120 --> 00:32:29,520
I have my way of working.

529
00:32:30,040 --> 00:32:31,240
What’s wrong with that?

530
00:32:34,440 --> 00:32:35,480
I never knew…

531
00:32:36,440 --> 00:32:39,880
this was how a top-selling AE worked.

532
00:32:41,320 --> 00:32:42,560
Enough.

533
00:32:43,720 --> 00:32:45,080
I want to see teamwork,

534
00:32:45,080 --> 00:32:47,920
not your fights.

535
00:32:49,720 --> 00:32:52,600
Could you please reconsider this assignment?

536
00:32:52,840 --> 00:32:54,680
I can’t work with a spoiled rich kid

537
00:32:55,080 --> 00:32:56,680
who’s here just for the social life,

538
00:32:56,800 --> 00:32:58,080
acts all high and mighty,

539
00:32:58,840 --> 00:33:00,600
and doesn’t care about his coworkers.

540
00:33:00,960 --> 00:33:01,600
Saint,

541
00:33:02,680 --> 00:33:03,920
why don't you take a break?

542
00:33:06,360 --> 00:33:07,120
Yes, P’Ta.

543
00:33:14,920 --> 00:33:15,680
Dan.

544
00:33:15,800 --> 00:33:16,880
What’s going on?

545
00:33:19,440 --> 00:33:20,960
I just can’t work with Saint.

546
00:33:21,920 --> 00:33:23,800
Everything he does annoys me.

547
00:33:25,320 --> 00:33:26,440
We have nothing in common.

548
00:33:27,080 --> 00:33:28,200
This won’t work.

549
00:33:28,880 --> 00:33:31,800
Have you even tried working with him?

550
00:33:32,320 --> 00:33:33,720
You’re smart.

551
00:33:33,720 --> 00:33:35,080
You’re the top seller.

552
00:33:35,560 --> 00:33:39,320
But try letting go of your perfectionism.

553
00:33:39,560 --> 00:33:43,040
New approaches and people

554
00:33:43,040 --> 00:33:45,600
can offer fresh perspectives.

555
00:33:45,600 --> 00:33:46,400
P’Ta,

556
00:33:46,600 --> 00:33:49,440
could you reconsider it, as Saint suggested?

557
00:33:50,840 --> 00:33:52,280
I’d rather give up this project

558
00:33:52,280 --> 00:33:53,400
and let Saint take it.

559
00:33:53,560 --> 00:33:54,920
That’s not an option.

560
00:33:55,160 --> 00:33:57,440
The client specifically requested you,

561
00:33:57,440 --> 00:33:59,080
so you have to handle it.

562
00:34:04,720 --> 00:34:07,520
I believe you can help Saint improve.

563
00:34:11,920 --> 00:34:14,120
I’m brain dead from work.

564
00:34:14,120 --> 00:34:15,520
I still have a lot to do.

565
00:34:18,320 --> 00:34:19,639
It’s Friday.

566
00:34:19,639 --> 00:34:22,280
Why don’t we take Saint out

567
00:34:22,400 --> 00:34:23,760
to celebrate passing probation?

568
00:34:25,520 --> 00:34:26,199
Good idea.

569
00:34:26,199 --> 00:34:28,040
Sounds fun.

570
00:34:28,360 --> 00:34:29,320
Then...

571
00:34:29,400 --> 00:34:30,840
Are you treating us, too?

572
00:34:31,960 --> 00:34:32,639
What do you say?

573
00:34:32,880 --> 00:34:34,000
Fine. My treat.

574
00:34:35,840 --> 00:34:36,800
Where are we going?

575
00:34:37,199 --> 00:34:39,080
Somewhere with karaoke.

576
00:34:39,080 --> 00:34:41,560
Someone wants to show off his singing skills.

577
00:34:43,120 --> 00:34:43,880
As for me,

578
00:34:44,080 --> 00:34:46,639
I’ll be happy with a cold beer.

579
00:34:46,639 --> 00:34:48,159
Oh.

580
00:34:48,159 --> 00:34:49,960
The main drinker.

581
00:34:49,960 --> 00:34:51,639
-Then I’m the main dancer.
-Okay.

582
00:34:51,960 --> 00:34:54,639
Cheers!

583
00:34:55,159 --> 00:34:56,719
You passed probation!

584
00:35:03,320 --> 00:35:07,280
Sing! Sing! Sing!

585
00:35:09,320 --> 00:35:10,120
Alright.

586
00:35:13,360 --> 00:35:15,560
He must be good.

587
00:35:18,680 --> 00:35:20,920
From zero to one hundred,

588
00:35:20,920 --> 00:35:24,880
I gave you a full hundred.

589
00:35:25,960 --> 00:35:26,880
You give him…

590
00:35:27,120 --> 00:35:29,200
Just give the mic back.

591
00:35:31,640 --> 00:35:33,160
He passed probation,

592
00:35:33,160 --> 00:35:34,640
not a singing audition.

593
00:35:34,640 --> 00:35:38,120
Without Dan, we don't have a main vocal.

594
00:35:38,360 --> 00:35:39,120
Exactly.

595
00:35:39,320 --> 00:35:39,880
Right?

596
00:35:39,880 --> 00:35:41,000
That’s right.

597
00:35:41,000 --> 00:35:42,280
If he were here,

598
00:35:42,280 --> 00:35:46,960
this room would be Impact Arena.

599
00:35:46,960 --> 00:35:48,360
True.

600
00:35:49,160 --> 00:35:49,920
Exactly.

601
00:35:52,960 --> 00:35:53,560
Ellie.

602
00:35:53,560 --> 00:35:54,920
Think before you speak.

603
00:35:55,360 --> 00:35:56,920
You always say things without thinking.

604
00:35:56,920 --> 00:35:57,760
What a nasty mouth.

605
00:35:57,760 --> 00:35:58,360
Hey!

606
00:35:59,120 --> 00:36:00,040
Bad personality.

607
00:36:01,080 --> 00:36:01,800
What?

608
00:36:02,360 --> 00:36:04,120
Cheers!

609
00:36:06,320 --> 00:36:07,240
Bottoms up!

610
00:36:07,560 --> 00:36:08,360
Let’s sing!

611
00:36:12,640 --> 00:36:14,080
I’m not good at singing.

612
00:36:15,840 --> 00:36:17,160
Then I’ll sing.

613
00:36:17,680 --> 00:36:19,480
From zero to one hundred,

614
00:36:19,480 --> 00:36:21,960
how many points would you give me?

615
00:36:21,960 --> 00:36:25,840
But I’d give you a full hundred with all my heart.

616
00:36:25,840 --> 00:36:28,840
Won’t you give me a chance?

617
00:36:28,840 --> 00:36:33,120
I’ll love you more than anyone else.

618
00:36:37,040 --> 00:36:37,880
I’m tired.

619
00:36:38,160 --> 00:36:38,840
Are you tired yet?

620
00:36:38,880 --> 00:36:39,880
I’m good. Keep going.

621
00:36:41,680 --> 00:36:44,440
We’re not old yet. Let’s keep going.

622
00:36:53,120 --> 00:36:55,960
Won’t you give me a chance?

623
00:37:07,640 --> 00:37:13,320
No matter what, I’ll love only you.

624
00:37:31,640 --> 00:37:32,400
I’m sorry.

625
00:37:36,560 --> 00:37:38,360
How many have you broken today?

626
00:37:47,360 --> 00:37:48,280
I’m sorry.

627
00:37:50,360 --> 00:37:51,360
Careful.

628
00:37:51,880 --> 00:37:52,720
Yes.

629
00:38:18,080 --> 00:38:19,320
Need a hand?

630
00:38:26,360 --> 00:38:27,120
Yes, please.

631
00:38:50,960 --> 00:38:51,800
Hey!

632
00:38:51,800 --> 00:38:54,800
They hired you to work, not to study!

633
00:39:00,160 --> 00:39:01,640
I don’t need this book anymore.

634
00:39:02,240 --> 00:39:03,120
Here, take it.

635
00:39:10,360 --> 00:39:11,360
Thank you.

636
00:39:13,960 --> 00:39:14,680
Hey!

637
00:39:24,720 --> 00:39:25,840
Watch out.

638
00:40:00,200 --> 00:40:01,360
Want me to tutor you?

639
00:40:01,360 --> 00:40:02,360
I can help you study.

640
00:40:07,720 --> 00:40:08,640
No, thank you.

641
00:40:09,120 --> 00:40:10,200
I can’t afford to pay you.

642
00:40:10,520 --> 00:40:12,040
I’ll do it for free.

643
00:40:12,440 --> 00:40:13,520
Which one you don’t understand?

644
00:40:15,920 --> 00:40:17,080
This one.

645
00:40:17,440 --> 00:40:18,760
Starting with the first question.

646
00:40:21,560 --> 00:40:24,320
Calculate the freezing point of the following solution.

647
00:40:26,120 --> 00:40:27,720
Which answer would you choose?

648
00:40:29,120 --> 00:40:31,720
I’d probably choose A.

649
00:40:32,120 --> 00:40:33,800
Because to calculate the freezing point,

650
00:40:33,800 --> 00:40:35,200
you need to use the delta T formula.

651
00:40:37,640 --> 00:40:38,440
Right?

652
00:40:38,720 --> 00:40:39,560
That’s right.

653
00:40:40,360 --> 00:40:41,360
See? You know the answer.

654
00:40:42,160 --> 00:40:43,360
I’m just not confident.

655
00:40:50,520 --> 00:40:52,360
P’James!

656
00:40:52,640 --> 00:40:54,240
I got into university!

657
00:41:08,080 --> 00:41:09,800
Congratulations, my good boy.

658
00:41:11,600 --> 00:41:12,920
Are you tired today?

659
00:41:13,360 --> 00:41:14,720
How’s university life?

660
00:41:15,440 --> 00:41:16,320
I’m not tired.

661
00:41:16,880 --> 00:41:18,360
I’ve been teaching for years.

662
00:41:19,640 --> 00:41:20,400
I’m used to it.

663
00:41:21,920 --> 00:41:23,960
But you’re teaching psychology at university.

664
00:41:24,360 --> 00:41:25,960
Teaching a subject that complicated

665
00:41:26,400 --> 00:41:27,800
must be exhausting sometimes.

666
00:41:31,040 --> 00:41:32,240
Whenever I’m tired,

667
00:41:33,360 --> 00:41:34,680
I’ll come see you.

668
00:41:35,120 --> 00:41:36,080
Just like today.

669
00:41:39,360 --> 00:41:40,720
That’ll make me feel better.

670
00:41:49,520 --> 00:41:51,120
I still remember this restaurant.

671
00:41:52,520 --> 00:41:55,800
You brought me here when my admission results came out.

672
00:41:57,320 --> 00:41:58,840
Now that I’m working,

673
00:41:59,440 --> 00:42:01,000
let me treat you.

674
00:42:01,280 --> 00:42:02,400
No way.

675
00:42:03,680 --> 00:42:05,760
I invited you, so I’m paying.

676
00:42:07,560 --> 00:42:09,280
You can treat me when you’re older.

677
00:42:09,640 --> 00:42:11,520
You’ve said that for almost ten years.

678
00:42:12,520 --> 00:42:14,120
Do you still see me as a kid?

679
00:42:15,440 --> 00:42:18,400
Do you still cry over getting one question wrong on a test?

680
00:42:24,320 --> 00:42:25,360
It’s okay.

681
00:42:28,520 --> 00:42:30,120
I’ll help you study next time.

682
00:42:30,960 --> 00:42:32,400
You’ll get a perfect score for sure.

683
00:42:50,600 --> 00:42:53,840
(I’m rooting for you. You can do it.)

684
00:42:58,520 --> 00:42:59,360
So…

685
00:43:01,320 --> 00:43:03,280
What are you crying about now?

686
00:43:08,920 --> 00:43:10,560
Happy Valentine’s Day, P’James.

687
00:43:11,440 --> 00:43:14,120
Another secret of mine is…

688
00:43:15,400 --> 00:43:16,880
I’ve been secretly in love with P’James

689
00:43:17,120 --> 00:43:18,720
for almost ten years.

690
00:43:19,360 --> 00:43:21,560
He’s almost everything to me.

691
00:43:21,720 --> 00:43:22,880
I…

692
00:43:23,040 --> 00:43:25,120
He changed my life.

693
00:43:26,440 --> 00:43:27,720
He’s my happiness.

694
00:43:28,960 --> 00:43:30,760
He can be everything I need.

695
00:43:36,040 --> 00:43:36,600
James.

696
00:43:50,920 --> 00:43:51,560
Let’s go.

697
00:43:54,760 --> 00:43:55,600
Everything except…

698
00:43:56,440 --> 00:43:57,160
my lover.

699
00:44:08,200 --> 00:44:09,840
Kimhan is coming back to Thailand.

700
00:44:13,160 --> 00:44:14,120
Why?

701
00:44:14,560 --> 00:44:15,880
Why is he suddenly coming back?

702
00:44:18,800 --> 00:44:21,720
He probably got tired of traveling on his parents’ money.

703
00:44:34,320 --> 00:44:35,600
Don’t worry, Dan.

704
00:44:36,920 --> 00:44:38,520
It’s been a long time.

705
00:44:39,320 --> 00:44:41,360
Kimhan won’t come into your life again.

706
00:44:44,200 --> 00:44:45,080
P’James…

707
00:44:45,640 --> 00:44:47,840
is still the one I can always rely on

708
00:44:48,360 --> 00:44:49,720
no matter what we’ve been through.

709
00:44:52,880 --> 00:44:55,000
I’m not afraid of Kimhan coming back into my life.

710
00:44:55,920 --> 00:44:58,320
I’m just afraid he’ll steal you from me again.

711
00:44:59,400 --> 00:45:01,960
And I don’t want to cry over you anymore.

712
00:45:04,120 --> 00:45:05,200
I like…

713
00:45:05,200 --> 00:45:06,560
Don’t be afraid, Dan.

714
00:45:09,000 --> 00:45:11,880
I won’t let Kimhan do anything to my little brother.

715
00:45:17,120 --> 00:45:17,840
P’James

716
00:45:18,360 --> 00:45:20,520
is the only one I want to tell my secret to.

717
00:45:21,800 --> 00:45:22,880
I love you.

718
00:45:23,920 --> 00:45:25,120
I love you, P’James.

719
00:45:25,840 --> 00:45:27,720
I don’t want to keep my love...

720
00:45:28,160 --> 00:45:29,800
a secret anymore.

721
00:46:15,360 --> 00:46:17,160
This project means a lot to me.

722
00:46:17,160 --> 00:46:18,480
It’s a big project,

723
00:46:18,480 --> 00:46:20,720
and my chance to prove myself.

724
00:46:20,720 --> 00:46:22,040
How about this?

725
00:46:22,440 --> 00:46:24,440
Let’s try to be good teammates.

726
00:46:24,720 --> 00:46:27,160
Tomorrow, we’ll meet the client at HQ.

727
00:46:27,160 --> 00:46:29,720
Every team, have your final sales files ready.

728
00:46:29,720 --> 00:46:32,920
Are you enjoying working with the spoiled Dan?

729
00:46:32,920 --> 00:46:34,560
Kimhan is coming back to Thailand.

730
00:46:36,400 --> 00:46:39,240
Is Mr. Kimhan what's bothering you?

731
00:46:39,240 --> 00:46:41,120
Please welcome our new CEO,

732
00:46:41,120 --> 00:46:42,160
Mr. Kimhan.

733
00:46:42,160 --> 00:46:43,080
Hello.
